This extension adds DOOM: The Dark Ages modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b][size=4][color=#ffff00]Supports Atlan Mod Loader and DarkAgesModManager! [/color](only Steam supported for now)[/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Atlan Mod Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "DarkAgesModManager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Atlan Resource Extractor installs to the game folder, recognised by an "AtlanResourceExtractor.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Valen mods with a "Valen.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]DarkAgesPatcher mods with a "DarkAgesPatcher.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Sound mods with a ".snd" or ".pck" file install to the "base\sound\soundbanks\pc" folder.[/*]
[*]Config mods with a ".cfg" file install to the "base" folder.[/*]
[*]Nested Archive mods are recognised by a "darkagesmod.txt" file.[/*]
[*]Binaries / Root Folder mods install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically creates an autoexec.cfg file and adds any .cfg files you install to execute from there.[/*]
[*][color=#f6b26b][b]Vortex will send a notification to run Atlan on each deployment. You must select the mods you want to load and their order in Atlan and launch the game from there to complete mod installation. You can launch the game normally on subsequent launches (no new mods).[/b][/color][/*]
[*]Includes buttons to open several useful files and folders (folder icon on Mods toolbar).[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for DOOM: The Dark Ages mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Atlan Mod Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "DarkAgesModManager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Atlan Resource Extractor:

Recognised when the archive contains a "AtlanResourceExtractor.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Valen:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Valen.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

DarkAgesPatcher:

Recognised when the archive contains a "DarkAgesPatcher.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Sound:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".snd" or ".pck" file.

  Installs to: "base\sound\soundbanks\pc"

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Configuration tweaks, deployed to the game's config location.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".cfg" extension.

  Installs to: "base"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod makes the whole archive install as a config mod.

========================================================================

Zip Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "darkagesmod.txt" file.

========================================================================

Binaries / Root Folder:

Handled by the "testBinaries" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

